        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ranchettescheyenneneighborhood.org/ranchettes-the-land-legacy-and-living-heritage-of-cheyenne-s-beloved-neighborhood/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Ranchettes describes small-scale ranch properties, typically between two and ten acres, designed for hobby farmers and horse enthusiasts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ranchettescheyenneneighborhood.org/ranchettes-the-land-legacy-and-living-heritage-of-cheyenne-s-beloved-neighborhood/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Developers created the Ranchettes to offer the independence of ranch life while remaining within reach of urban amenities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ranchettescheyenneneighborhood.org/ranchettes-the-land-legacy-and-living-heritage-of-cheyenne-s-beloved-neighborhood/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early subdivisions of the Ranchettes were first carved out along Ridge Road and Four Mile Road during the 1950s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ranchettescheyenneneighborhood.org/ranchettes-the-land-legacy-and-living-heritage-of-cheyenne-s-beloved-neighborhood/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Four Mile Road serves as a symbolic thoroughfare linking small acreages and scenic views from the city edge toward Horse Creek.",
